---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const clone = `git clone https://github.com/wrbl606/fleet.git
cd fleet`;

const core = `python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python3 -m fleetctl env-check --platform linux`;

const registry = `# write deployment-specific routing to the git-ignored overlay
scripts/configure-registry.sh jira --project ENG --repo acme/engine --labels agent
scripts/configure-registry.sh trusted acme/engine
scripts/configure-registry.sh show --effective   # merged view`;

const panel = `mise install
bash admin/start.sh --host 0.0.0.0 --port 4000`;

const smudge = `bash scripts/smoke.sh     # expected: PASS`;

const checks = `bash scripts/ci.sh         # fleetctl unit tests + schema validation
bash scripts/ci-admin.sh   # admin: compile --warnings-as-errors + format + tests`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Installation"
  description="Install fleet: prerequisites, the fleetctl dispatcher core, the trusted registry, the Phoenix admin panel, and Jenkins."
>
  <div class="docs-prose">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-primary/80">installation</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-base-content sm:text-4xl">Installation</h1>
    <p class="text-lg">
      fleet is glue, not a package: a host runs from a git checkout plus a state directory and the
      external tools it already uses. Install the pieces you need — the dispatcher core and panel
      run without Jenkins.
    </p>

    <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Python 3.11+</strong> and <code>pip</code> (PyYAML + jsonschema).</li>
      <li><strong>git</strong> and the <strong>GitHub CLI</strong> (<code>gh</code>) on the runner host.</li>
      <li><strong>Linux runners (COI):</strong> Incus and <code>coi</code>, with your user in <code>incus-admin</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Admin panel / website:</strong> Erlang &amp; Elixir (admin) through <a href="https://mise.jdx.dev/">mise</a>, Node (website), pinned in the repo <code>mise.toml</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Jenkins</strong> controller + build nodes (installed separately).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>1. Get the code</h2>
    <pre><code>{clone}</code></pre>

    <h2>2. Dispatcher core</h2>
    <p>
      <code>fleetctl</code> owns normalize → resolve → plan → run → publish. It is stdlib-first and
      runs identically on a laptop and in CI.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{core}</code></pre>

    <h2>3. Trusted registry</h2>
    <p>
      Keep the tracked <code>registry.yaml</code> generic and write deployment-specific routing,
      allowlists, and comment policy to the git-ignored <code>registry.local.yaml</code> overlay.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{registry}</code></pre>

    <h2>4. Admin panel</h2>
    <p>
      The panel owns the run ledger and the webhook ingest endpoint. It defaults to{" "}
      <code>0.0.0.0:4000</code> and migrates the database on start.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{panel}</code></pre>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Env var</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>FLEET_INGEST_TOKEN</code></td><td>Bearer token for <code>POST /api/ingest</code>, <code>POST /api/trigger</code>, and <code>GET /api/metrics</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>FLEET_WEBHOOK_URL</code></td><td>Dispatcher endpoint inbound webhooks are forwarded to (Jenkins GWT invoke URL)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>FLEET_WEBHOOK_TOKEN</code></td><td>Token appended to the forward URL and sent as a bearer header</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>FLEET_INGEST_PUBLIC_URL</code></td><td>Public URL of the panel ingest endpoint, shown on the Trigger page</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>FLEET_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code></td><td>GitHub webhook secret for <code>X-Hub-Signature-256</code> HMAC auth</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>FLEET_JENKINS_URL</code></td><td>Jenkins master web UI, linked from the nav and Trigger page</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code></td><td>GitOps config PRs (<code>contents:write</code>, <code>pull-requests:write</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>FLEET_ADMIN_USER</code> / <code>FLEET_ADMIN_PASSWORD</code></td><td>Optional HTTP Basic auth for the UI</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Pages: <code>/</code> run ledger, <code>/ingest</code> ingest log, <code>/trigger</code> manual trigger, <code>/gitops</code> config PRs.</p>

    <h2>5. Jenkins</h2>
    <p>
      Jenkins is <strong>not bundled</strong>. The dispatcher core and panel run without it, but the
      webhook → pipeline → PR flow needs a Jenkins you operate. For a local WAR install use the
      helper scripts; otherwise install the plugins from <code>scripts/jenkins/plugins.txt</code>,
      add this repo as a global shared library named <code>fleet-config</code>, provide nodes
      labeled{" "}
      <code>fleet-agent</code>, and create the credentials{" "}
      <code>fleet-webhook-token</code>, <code>fleet-github-read</code>,
      <code>fleet-github-token</code>, and one per <code>[agent].llm_env</code>. See{" "}
      <a data-astro-prefetch href="/docs/triggers">Triggers &amp; ingest</a> for the webhook wiring.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Landing page (optional)</h2>
    <p>The marketing site is a static Astro build in <code>website/</code>.</p>
    <pre><code>{`bash website/start.sh            # dev server on 0.0.0.0:4100
bash website/start.sh --build    # production build + preview
bash website/start.sh --daemon   # background; stop with website/stop.sh`}</code></pre>

    <h2>7. Verify</h2>
    <p>Run the sandbox smoke test (no LLM key required) and the CI checks.</p>
    <pre><code>{smudge}

{checks}</code></pre>

    <h2>Next</h2>
    <p>
      Configure how tasks enter fleet in <a data-astro-prefetch href="/docs/triggers">Triggers &amp; ingest</a>, or read
      the <a href="https://github.com/wrbl606/fleet/blob/main/docs/security.md">security model</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
